---
import BlockLayout from '../../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import guide from '../../data/ai-work-life.json';
const categories = [...new Set(guide.plans.map(p=>p.area))];
const dollars = (n:number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD'});
const jsonLd = {'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Article',headline:guide.title,description:guide.dek,datePublished:guide.asOf,author:{'@type':'Organization',name:'PointCast — Codex research and writing'},editor:{'@type':'Person',name:'Mike Hoydich'},publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'PointCast'},image:'https://pointcast.xyz/images/ai-work-life/hero.png',mainEntityOfPage:'https://pointcast.xyz/reviews/ai-work-life'};
---
<BlockLayout title={guide.title} description={guide.dek} image="/images/ai-work-life/hero.png" jsonLd={jsonLd} immersive>
<main class="ai-guide">
<nav class="mast" aria-label="PointCast"><a href="/">POINTCAST <span>/ SHOP NOTES</span></a><a href="/reviews">Reviews ↗</a><a href="/shop/front">Shop ↗</a></nav>
<header class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE AI BUYING GUIDE / SEPTEMBER 2026</p><h1>A little<br/>more<br/><em>possible.</em></h1><p class="dek">Which AI plan is worth paying for? Start with the thing you want to do.</p><p class="byline">Editorial direction: <strong>Mike Hoydich</strong><br/>Research & writing: Codex · September 29, 2026</p><a class="button" href="#plans">Find your plan ↓</a></div><figure><img src="/images/ai-work-life/hero.svg" width="1200" height="1000" alt="An editorial diagram of an idea becoming a draft, a prototype and a reviewed result" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>EDITORIAL GRAPHIC · POSSIBILITY STILL NEEDS PRACTICE.</figcaption></figure></header>
<div class="ribbon"><span>22 SERVICES</span><span>14 AREAS</span><span>07 MODELS</span><span>00 PAID LINKS</span></div>
<nav class="contents" aria-label="Guide contents"><a href="#start">Start here</a><a href="#areas">What can it do?</a><a href="#plans">Plans & prices</a><a href="#models">Best models for the job</a><a href="#calculator">Is it worth it?</a></nav>
<aside class="companion">Looking for every tier and agent allowance? <a href="/reviews/ai-plans">Read our companion subscription guide →</a></aside>
<section id="start" class="intro section"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE POINTCAST TAKE</p><h2>Buy one useful<br/>new habit.</h2></div><div><p>The interesting part of access to powerful models is how many things become cheap enough to try. A question can become a research brief. A sketch can become a working prototype. A difficult paragraph can get five different openings before lunch.</p><p>That changes the cost of a first attempt. It does not remove the work of deciding what matters, recognizing a weak answer or finishing something people can use.</p><p><strong>Our starting recommendation: use a free tier, then choose one general plan around $20 a month if you repeatedly hit a useful limit.</strong> Add a specialist only when you can name the recurring step it improves. The best model is the one that helps you get an acceptable result with the least total cost—including your review time.</p></div></section>
<section class="section vocabulary"><p class="eyebrow">FOUR DIFFERENT PURCHASES</p><div class="four"><article><span>01 / MODEL</span><h3>The engine.</h3><p>GPT, Claude and Gemini model names describe systems with different abilities, costs and limits.</p></article><article><span>02 / SUBSCRIPTION</span><h3>The workspace.</h3><p>A monthly app plan bundles a user interface, tools and allowances. It may offer several models.</p></article><article><span>03 / SPECIALIST</span><h3>The workflow.</h3><p>A legal, design or marketing product adds context and process. It may use the same underlying models.</p></article><article><span>04 / API</span><h3>The meter.</h3><p>Software pays for usage. Tokens, search, media and other tools can have separate charges.</p></article></div><p class="fine">Similar output does not make two products equivalent. Permissions, integrations, retention settings, team controls and the work needed to review a result all affect the purchase.</p></section>
<section id="areas" class="section"><p class="eyebrow">FROM ABSTRACT POWER TO A REAL AFTERNOON</p><h2>What could move forward?</h2><p class="lead">A starting map across work and life. Open the area you care about.</p><div class="areas">{guide.areas.map((a,i)=><details><summary><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span>{a.name}<b aria-hidden="true">+</b></summary><p>{a.workflow}</p><p><strong>Start with:</strong> {a.start}</p><p class="checkpoint"><strong>Human checkpoint:</strong> {a.checkpoint}</p></details>)}</div></section>
<section id="plans" class="section plans"><p class="eyebrow">THE SHOPPING SHELF</p><h2>A plan for the job.<br/><em>Not every plan.</em></h2><p class="lead">These are representative options worth comparing, not every AI product on sale. Prices are a dated snapshot; the linked provider page is the buying destination.</p><aside class="note">{guide.disclosure} We have not tested all these products. There are no sponsored placements or star ratings.</aside><div class="toolbar"><label for="plan-search">Find a service or use case<input id="plan-search" type="search" placeholder="Try legal, coding, voice…" /></label><label for="plan-category">Area<select id="plan-category" aria-label="Area"><option value="all">All areas</option>{categories.map(c=><option value={c}>{c}</option>)}</select></label></div><p id="plan-count" aria-live="polite" class="fine">Showing all {guide.plans.length} services.</p><div class="plan-grid">{guide.plans.map((p,i)=><article class="plan" id={p.id} data-area={p.area} data-search={`${p.name} ${p.area} ${p.why} ${p.alternative}`.toLowerCase()}><div class="card-top"><span>{p.area}</span><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span></div><h3>{p.name}</h3><p class="price">{p.priceText}</p><p>{p.why}</p><p class="catch"><strong>The catch.</strong> {p.catch}</p><p class="alternative"><strong>Compare with</strong><br/>{p.alternative}</p><a class="shop-link" href={p.url} rel="noopener noreferrer">Official plans & buying details ↗</a><span class="fine">Direct link · no commission</span></article>)}</div><p id="no-results" hidden>No services match that search. Try another term or choose all areas.</p></section>
<section id="models" class="section models"><p class="eyebrow">THE ENGINE ROOM</p><h2>“Best” needs<br/>a second word.</h2><p class="lead">Best for what? A difficult contract question, a thousand short classifications and a visual mood board are different tests.</p><p>For text and code, these seven models form a useful comparison set. The roles below are editorial judgments informed by provider documentation, not a PointCast benchmark. Image, video and voice systems have different outputs and billing units; compare them through the specialist workflows above.</p><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="API model price comparison"><table><caption>Standard uncached API rates in USD per 1 million tokens · checked September 29, 2026</caption><thead><tr><th>Model / role</th><th>Input</th><th>Output</th><th>100 example jobs*</th></tr></thead><tbody>{guide.models.map(m=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={m.url}>{m.name} ↗</a><small>{m.role}</small></th><td>{dollars(m.input)}</td><td>{dollars(m.output)}</td><td>{dollars((m.input*.02+m.output*.004)*100)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="fine">*Each hypothetical job uses 20,000 input tokens and 4,000 billed output tokens. Output may include billed reasoning tokens. No cache, batch discount, retries, search, media, storage, tax or orchestration is included. Equal token counts do not mean equal results. Gemini’s listed $0.75 / $3.75 rates apply through December 31, 2026; its published January 2027 rates double.</p><div class="model-notes">{guide.models.map(m=><article><h3>{m.name}</h3><p>{m.why}</p></article>)}</div><aside class="note"><strong>App access ≠ API access.</strong> A subscription’s model menu and limits may differ from the API catalog. In particular, <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/15424964-claude-fable-models-on-your-plan">Fable has plan-specific credit rules</a>. Check the model and allowance you need before upgrading.</aside><h3 class="subhead">The equivalent is a finished job.</h3><p>A small model that correctly handles a routine task can be a better purchase than a premium model. A stronger model can be cheaper overall if it avoids an hour of repair. Compare ten representative examples: acceptance rate, factual errors, review minutes, latency and total bill. Give each candidate the same source material and a clear definition of success.</p><p>Open-weight models are another route if you can operate them. Access to weights does not eliminate hardware, hosting, security or maintenance costs. Privacy also depends on where and how you run the system. For most people choosing a first plan, an existing hosted tool is a simpler experiment.</p></section>
<section id="calculator" class="section calculator"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSONAL MATH</p><h2>What would<br/>make it worth it?</h2><p>Estimate capacity, not promised income. Saved time only becomes money if you can actually redeploy it.</p><p class="fine">Use incremental hours saved compared with how you work today. Subtract checking and repair time. Subscription and extra usage costs recur even in a quiet month.</p></div><form id="value-form"><div class="inputs"><label>Monthly plan cost ($)<input name="cost" type="number" min="0" max="100000" step="0.01" value="20" required /></label><label>Extra usage / seats ($)<input name="extras" type="number" min="0" max="100000" step="0.01" value="0" required /></label><label>Hours saved / month<input name="hours" type="number" min="0" max="744" step="0.1" value="3" required /></label><label>Review & repair hours<input name="review" type="number" min="0" max="744" step="0.1" value="1" required /></label><label>Value of your hour ($)<input name="rate" type="number" min="0" max="100000" step="0.01" value="50" required /></label></div><output id="value-result" aria-live="polite"><strong>$80</strong> estimated net monthly capacity value.<small>2.0 net hours reclaimed. Break-even: 24 net minutes/month at $50/hour.</small></output><p class="fine">Formula: (hours saved − review hours) × hourly value − plan and extra costs. This is an editable hypothetical, not a return forecast.</p></form></section>
<section class="section stacks"><p class="eyebrow">THREE SENSIBLE STARTS</p><h2>Keep the stack small.</h2><div class="three"><article><span class="stack-price">$0</span><h3>The curious start.</h3><p>Try free general tools on real, low-sensitivity tasks. Keep the one that helps you finish something. Learn its limits before adding a bill.</p></article><article><span class="stack-price">~$20<span>/mo</span></span><h3>One good workbench.</h3><p>Choose ChatGPT Plus, Claude Pro or Google AI Pro for your actual mix of work. Compare outputs and workflow; do not assume you need all three.</p></article><article><span class="stack-price">$45<span>/mo</span></span><h3>A visual experiment.</h3><p>One $20 general plan, $10 Midjourney Basic and $15 Runway Standard at monthly rates. Add the specialists only if you repeatedly need their outputs; allowances and extra usage still apply.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="closing section"><p class="eyebrow">WHY THIS IS INTERESTING</p><h2>More attempts.<br/>Better questions.<br/><em>Something finished.</em></h2><p>The opportunity is not to collect access badges. It is to do work you used to postpone: build a small tool, understand a dense document, rehearse a difficult conversation, or test an idea before spending a week on it.</p><p>Choose one real task. Give it good material. Make a first attempt. Check the result. Keep the part that helps. That is a much better reason to subscribe than a model name at the top of a leaderboard.</p><details><summary>Method, attribution & price notes</summary><p>{guide.method}</p><p>Mike Hoydich supplied the editorial direction and requested this guide. Codex researched and wrote it. This attribution does not claim that Mike personally tested or endorsed every product. We received no review access or compensation for this guide.</p><p>{guide.disclosure} “From” prices are entry points rather than a complete bill. Where regional localization, checkout-only pricing or a sales process prevented a firm US quote, the card says so. No affiliate account or tracking code is attached.</p><p>Provider descriptions establish availability and advertised capabilities; the recommendations, comparison paths and examples are our editorial synthesis. Prices and model names can change quickly. Re-check a provider’s page before payment, including renewal, cancellation, seats, usage and data settings.</p><p>Additional checks: <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11049762-choose-a-claude-plan">Claude plan tiers</a> · <a href="https://help.jasper.ai/hc/en-us/articles/18618709412123-Annual-Plans">Jasper annual billing</a> · <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model">OpenAI model guide</a>.</p><a href="/reviews/ai-work-life.json">Read the complete guide as JSON ↗</a></details><a href="/shop/front">Explore the shop →</a><a href="/reviews">More reviews →</a></section>
</main>
</BlockLayout>
<script>
function init(){
 const root=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.ai-guide');if(!root||root.dataset.ready)return;root.dataset.ready='true';
 const search=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#plan-search')!;const category=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#plan-category')!;
 const filter=()=>{let count=0;const query=search.value.trim().toLowerCase();root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.plan').forEach(card=>{card.hidden=!(category.value==='all'||card.dataset.area===category.value)||!card.dataset.search?.includes(query);if(!card.hidden)count++;});root.querySelector('#plan-count')!.textContent=`Showing ${count} of 22 services.`;root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#no-results')!.hidden=count!==0;};search.addEventListener('input',filter);category.addEventListener('change',filter);
 const form=root.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#value-form')!;const output=root.querySelector<HTMLOutputElement>('#value-result')!;
 const calculate=()=>{const names=['cost','extras','hours','review','rate'];const fields=names.map(n=>form.elements.namedItem(n) as HTMLInputElement);if(fields.some(f=>!f.validity.valid||!Number.isFinite(f.valueAsNumber))){output.textContent='Enter a valid, non-negative number in every field.';return;}const [cost,extras,hours,review,rate]=fields.map(f=>f.valueAsNumber);const net=hours-review;const value=net*rate-cost-extras;const amount=document.createElement('strong');amount.textContent=value.toLocaleString('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD',maximumFractionDigits:0});const detail=document.createElement('small');detail.textContent=`${net.toFixed(1)} net hours reclaimed. `+(rate>0?`Break-even: ${Math.ceil((cost+extras)/rate*60)} net minutes/month at $${rate}/hour.`:'Set a positive hourly value to calculate break-even time.');output.replaceChildren(amount,document.createTextNode(' estimated net monthly capacity value.'),detail);};form.addEventListener('input',calculate);form.addEventListener('submit',e=>e.preventDefault());calculate();
}init();document.addEventListener('astro:page-load',init);
</script>
<style>
